This package is a local mathematical extraction of the maximum-entropy Doppler
mapping method described by H. C. Spruit (1998), with real U Gem spectra supplied
through the pydoppler author repository. Upstream code and complete source
archives are kept separately for maintainer verification.

The Python wrapper repository contains an MIT license template naming the Python
Packaging Authority. This does not establish that the historical Spruit Fortran
implementation or observational spectra carry that license. The original
Fortran identifies H. C. Spruit and its historical version. No explicit
redistribution license for that Fortran or these spectra was established.
Permission for public redistribution remains unresolved; no MIT or Creative
Commons grant for those materials is asserted here. The present verification
and extraction were performed for the user's authorized local research.

The full original notices, exact source hashes, data provenance, minimum
environment adapters and failed runs are indexed in test/validation.md.
